    THE_HONEST_LCDM_STRESS_BRIEF.md:69 lists S_8 on the DO-NOT-CITE list -- as a LambdaCDM stress, because
    KiDS-Legacy and HSC-Y3 moved UP toward Planck.  That is a warning against claiming a low-S_8 deficit.
    It cuts BOTH ways here: the upward revision makes the shear constraint LESS hostile to a high-sigma_8
    model, so this lane uses KiDS-Legacy and the 2026 compilation as the primary shear comparison rather
    than the older, lower KiDS-1000 and DES Y3, which would manufacture a harsher verdict.
    NOTE on eRASS1: the same repository (routeB_dynamical_mass_calibration_eta.py:184-197) records that
    eRASS1's HIGH S_8 may be a weak-lensing mass-calibration artefact, and this lane's own L18 shows the
    hydrostatic bias runs against the framework.  eRASS1 is reported, not leaned on.

