============================================================================================================================
  C6 -- the coefficient question: kappa_closure/k03 vs L9's cosmology
============================================================================================================================
    k03 established that the framework's own relation a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) scales as H0 at fixed
    Omega_Lambda, so 'the coefficient is degenerate with the H0 tension': kappa = 1/2 on Planck's H0 and
    kappa = 0.461 on SH0ES's H0 give the same a0 to better than 1%.  L9's cosmology does NOT hold
    Omega_Lambda fixed -- the closure 1 = F(Omega_m + Omega_r + Omega_Lambda) forces it DOWN to 0.25-0.32.
    Since rho_Lambda is proportional to omega_Lambda = Omega_Lambda h^2, that is a first-order change in a0.
    canonical: omega_Lambda 0.1179-0.1418 against LambdaCDM 0.3107 (a factor 0.379-0.456)
      reading 1, the G in a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_L) is the LOCAL G_0:
        a0 would move by a factor 0.616-0.676, i.e. -38.4% to -32.4% (0.210-0.170 dex), against a 9.47% BTFR floor and DR4's 21% reach
        to hold a0 at its measured value the coefficient must be kappa = 0.740-0.812, which is 3.6-6.1 sigma from the two measured values (0.465 +/- 0.076 and 0.551 +/- 0.043)
      reading 2, that G is the COSMOLOGICAL F G_0 (the roll enters rho_Lambda's gravity too):
        a0 moves by 0.831-0.911 (-16.9% to -8.9%), and kappa = 0.549-0.602 (0.1-1.8 sigma)
    alt      : omega_Lambda 0.1269-0.1671 against LambdaCDM 0.3107 (a factor 0.408-0.538)
      reading 1, the G in a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_L) is the LOCAL G_0:
        a0 would move by a factor 0.639-0.733, i.e. -36.1% to -26.7% (0.194-0.135 dex), against a 9.47% BTFR floor and DR4's 21% reach
        to hold a0 at its measured value the coefficient must be kappa = 0.682-0.782, which is 2.9-5.4 sigma from the two measured values (0.465 +/- 0.076 and 0.551 +/- 0.043)
      reading 2, that G is the COSMOLOGICAL F G_0 (the roll enters rho_Lambda's gravity too):
        a0 moves by 0.828-0.951 (-17.2% to -4.9%), and kappa = 0.526-0.604 (0.6-1.8 sigma)

    fraction of the surviving region that keeps a0 inside k03's 9.47% BTFR mass-budget floor:
      canonical  reading 1 (local G):     0/146      reading 2 (cosmological G):   18/146
      alt        reading 1 (local G):     0/269      reading 2 (cosmological G):   96/269
