    HOW MUCH the roll would have to be removed from lensing for reading (i)/(i') to be legitimate.
    The largest S_8 that stays within 2 sigma of KiDS-Legacy is 0.8492, so the shear-kernel roll factor
    would have to satisfy g_eff <= that divided by the model's own no-roll amplitude:
      canonical: allowed g_eff <= 1.006-1.024 against the actual 1.338-1.441, i.e. the roll must be suppressed in the LENSING
                 potential by 94-98% relative to the DYNAMICAL one.
      alt      : allowed g_eff <= 1.000-1.028 against the actual 1.273-1.415, i.e. the roll must be suppressed in the LENSING
                 potential by 92-100% relative to the DYNAMICAL one.
    A suppression that large is exactly a lensing/dynamics decoupling of order F, and the same decoupling
    would make cluster weak-lensing masses disagree with X-ray hydrostatic masses by of order F ~ 1.7-1.8.
    They are observed to agree to tens of percent (L9's own open item (ii)), so this escape is not free.
  [FAIL] C7 [verdict] the late-roll mechanism survives current data on the reading that is SELF-CONSISTENT for a spatially uniform g(z), namely with the roll multiplying the Weyl potential that lenses light   (canonical: 0/146, alt: 0/269.  On the maximally favourable reading, where an unspecified screening removes the roll from the shear signal entirely, canonical: 57/146, alt: 58/269 survive, so the mechanism is ALIVE ONLY IN A CORNER and only under that assumption)

============================================================================================================================
  THE VERDICT OF THIS LANE
============================================================================================================================
  1. sigma_8 = 0.845-0.861 is high, but S_8 is NOT, and that is the first real finding.  L9's survivors
     carry Omega_m = 0.274-0.315, at or below the concordance 0.3153, so S_8 = sigma_8 sqrt(Omega_m/0.3) turns the high
     sigma_8 into S_8 = 0.808-0.882, which STRADDLES Planck's 0.832 +/- 0.013.  It sits +1.2 to +5.8 sigma from the older
     shear values (KiDS-1000, DES Y3, HSC Y3) but within 2 sigma of the revised KiDS-Legacy 0.815 +/- 0.016
     over most of the region, and inside 1 sigma of DESI DR9 lensing and eRASS1 cluster counts.  So the
     naive reading is NOT a kill: the S_8 tension running the other way does not by itself close it.
     One caveat AGAINST the model, from its own numbers: the naive formula discounts by Omega_m while the
     Weyl source carries the CMB-fixed omega_m, so the physically correct no-roll amplitude is HIGHER,
     S_8 = 0.828-0.851 -- the Omega_m discount is partly an artefact of the parametrisation.
  2. The kill is elsewhere, and it is the gate L9 said it did not run.  In MODEL A the roll multiplies the
     Poisson source, so with no slip it multiplies the Weyl potential.  The cosmic-shear amplitude is then
     larger than LambdaCDM's by the kernel-weighted g_eff = 1.27-1.44, giving an effective S_8 = 1.06-1.20
     against measurements at 0.76-0.86 with errors of 0.01-0.03.  That is not a tension, it is an exclusion
     by tens of sigma, and it does not depend on which shear survey is used.
  3. The escape is exactly the thing L9's own T8 already showed is unavailable.  Reading (i) survives only
     if a screening removes the roll from the shear signal while leaving it in the cluster masses -- i.e.
     the density-dependent screening L6 excluded at 12.8 sigma with 100% baryon-density overlap.  So the
     two halves close on each other: with the screening, L6 kills it; without it, cosmic shear does.
  4. And the framework's own coefficient moves with it.  L9's closure drives omega_Lambda down by a factor
     0.38-0.54, so a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) moves by -38% to -27% if the G in that
     relation is the LOCAL one -- outside k03's 9.47% BTFR floor at EVERY surviving point, and outside
     DR4's 21% reach as well -- or -17% to -5% if it is the COSMOLOGICAL F G_0, which stays
     inside the floor for 18/146 canonical and 96/269 alt points.  Holding a0 fixed on the first reading would need
     kappa = 0.68-0.81, 2.9-6.1 sigma from both measured values.  This is a NEW constraint and not a restatement
     of k03: k03's degeneracy was with H0 at FIXED Omega_Lambda, and L9's closure is precisely a mechanism
     that MOVES Omega_Lambda.  Which G enters is not settled here, so both readings are carried.
  5. What this does NOT show.  It does not rescue anything and it does not close the cluster problem, which
     L9's T8 already left fatal on its own terms.  It does not exclude a NON-uniform or non-monotone
     coupling, or a model where the lensing and dynamical potentials differ -- but such a model is no longer
     the MODEL A tested here, owes an action, and inherits L9's own item (ii): if lensing and hydrostatic
     cluster masses differ by of order F they are observed to agree to tens of percent.

  WHAT DRIVES EACH FAIL, stated so nothing is over-read: C2, C3, C4, C5 and C7 all fail on reading (ii)
  and ONLY on reading (ii).  On reading (i)/(i') -- the roll removed from the shear signal -- every one of
  them passes, and the mechanism is alive in a corner:
    canonical corner: z_t <= 0.132, W in [0.461, 0.521]  (57/146 of L9's region)
              sigma_8 0.853-0.856, S_8 0.818-0.833, H0 71.0-72.0, Omega_m 0.276-0.284, Omega_Lambda 0.266-0.274
    alt       corner: z_t <= 0.180, W in [0.441, 0.527]  (58/269 of L9's region)
              sigma_8 0.845-0.849, S_8 0.808-0.826, H0 71.0-72.2, Omega_m 0.274-0.284, Omega_Lambda 0.311-0.321
  C6 fails on its own terms and independently of the lensing question.

RESULT: 6 FAIL -> ["C2 [2 sigma] some part of L9's surviving region is compatible with the cosmic-shear S_8 at 2 sigma on EVERY reading of the model, including the one that is self-consistent for a spatially uniform g(z)", "C3 [3 sigma] some part of L9's surviving region is compatible with the cosmic-shear S_8 at 3 sigma on EVERY reading of the model, including the one that is self-consistent for a spatially uniform g(z)", 'C4 [H0+S8] a SINGLE surviving point sits within 2 sigma of a measured H0 (Planck or SH0ES) and within 2 sigma of the most favourable modern cosmic-shear S_8 at the same time, on EVERY reading', "C5 [growth on real data] with L9's internal Delta chi^2 gate replaced by the absolute goodness of fit to the RSD points and by the measured S_8, part of the region still survives on EVERY reading", "C6 [kappa] L9's surviving cosmology leaves the framework's own a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) relation intact -- every surviving point stays inside the 9.47% BTFR mass-budget floor that k03 identified as the precision limit, on both readings of which G enters", 'C7 [verdict] the late-roll mechanism survives current data on the reading that is SELF-CONSISTENT for a spatially uniform g(z), namely with the roll multiplying the Weyl potential that lenses light']
